# CatDex — Security

## Secrets

- Never commit API keys, service role keys, JWT secrets
- Client: only `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` non-secret config
- Server: `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET` in server env only

## AuthZ

- RLS on `profiles`, `cats`, `sightings`, `cat_analysis` — users touch own rows (and documented shared sighting rules)
- Analyze endpoint verifies Supabase JWT (unless explicit unsafe dev flag)
- Rate-limit analyze on server

## Uploads

- Validate image types/sizes server-side where enforced
- Don’t log base64 photo payloads
- Storage paths should not be guessable across users without policy checks

## UX safety

- Error messages: actionable, no stack traces or env dumps in UI
- OAuth: use configured redirect URLs only

## Checklist before commit

- [ ] No hardcoded secrets
- [ ] User inputs validated (`authValidation`, Vision schema)
- [ ] RLS / JWT assumptions unchanged or migrated safely
